## 6. The lang attribute
   concept: <html lang> tells screen readers which voice and hyphenation to use (WCAG 3.1.1); a passage in another language carries its own lang (3.1.2)
   / (en): <html lang="en">, switcher <a href="/?member=alice&amp;lang=fr" hreflang="fr" lang="fr">Français</a>
   / (fr): <html lang="fr">, switcher <a href="/?member=alice&amp;lang=en" hreflang="en" lang="en">English</a>
   /naive (fr): <html> without lang, so a screen reader reads the French page with the user's default voice

